          "target": "The LRC(n) runner-recursion angle: (1) factorization table of C=2n-1 with n=14 -> C=27=3^3 as the unique non-trivial prime power in n=8..20; (2) AP-to-cap margin on the uniform binding row |P|=5, with n=14 tightest (+0.054); (3) closed-form recursion p_all-missed(consec_k) = 1/(s(k-1)), s=n/2, exact for all even n and all k.",
          "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
          "evidence": "I reimplemented both kernels from scratch with fractions.Fraction (independent breakpoint derivation), in C:\\Users\\Eliott\\Documents\\GitHub\\math\\04-computation\\lrc_runner_adversarial_verify.py and lrc_runner_margin_adversarial.py.\n\nENGINE VALIDATION (my code reproduces canon exactly): my from-scratch meas_GP gives cap_8(n=14)=2243/5880 EXACTLY (=0.381463, matches THM-530), bestP=(1,5,7,8,9); meas_S(consec_8,s=7)=481/1470 EXACTLY; p_all-missed(consec_8,s=7)=1/49 EXACTLY. These are the three canonical anchors and all match.\n\nCLAIM 1 (factorization) CONFIRMED. My independent trial-division factoring of C=2n-1: n=8->15=3*5, 10->19, 12->23, 14->27=3^3, 16->31, 18->35=5*7, 20->39=3*13. n=14 is the UNIQUE non-trivial prime power (maxexp 3); 10/12/16 are trivial prime powers (primes), 8/18/20 are squarefree composites. Exactly as claimed.\n\nCLAIM 3 (recursion 1/(s(k-1))) CONFIRMED. Tested all even n=8..20 and all k=2..n-1 (84 cases): ZERO mismatches between p_all-missed(consec_k,s=n/2) and the exact Fraction 1/(s(k-1)).\n\nCLAIM 2 (|P|=5 margin, n=14 tightest) CONFIRMED with one refinement. Exhaustive min of meas_GP over ALL speed subsets {1..n-1} of size 5 (not the canon script's restricted search) gives margins: n=8 +0.0732, n=10 +0.2038, n=12 +0.1919, n=14 +0.0543 (TIGHTEST), n=16 +0.1276, n=18 +0.1003, n=20 +0.1364. These match the claimed +0.073/+0.204/+0.192/+0.054/+0.128/+0.100/+0.136. n=14 is genuinely the tightest non-degenerate row. REFINEMENT/CAVEAT: the literal sub-claim \"only n=14 squeezes below 0.10\" is false at |P|=5 because n=8 is also +0.073<0.10 -- but n=8 is degenerate (k=2 cluster {0,1} gives meas_S(AP)=0, an empty cover), which the claim itself flagged; among non-degenerate rows n=14 is uniquely <0.10 (next is n=18 at +0.1003). My exhaustive caps at n=16/18/20 are slightly SMALLER than the canon restricted-search caps (e.g. n=16 0.44803 vs 0.44911), which only tightens margins toward the claim, never away.\n\nDECOUPLING table CONFIRMED exactly: E={0,1,2,3}+{0,d}, meas_S(s=7) = 0.08214(d=5),0.07880(6),0.09110(7),0.09513(8),0.11329(12),0.11393(d=100); all << cap_8=0.381, matching claimed 0.082/0.079/0.091/0.095/0.113/0.114 and stabilizing ~0.11 (Freiman-dim-2 GAP low-coverage regime).\n\nOutputs saved: 05-knowledge/results/lrc_runner_margin_adversarial.out. The divisor-lattice mechanism claim (2) is structural/interpretive (chain 1|3|9|27 vs Boolean cubes); the numerical backbone it rests on (n=14 uniquely tight + unique prime power) is verified, so the correlation is real, though \"lattice shape causes tightness\" remains an interpretation rather than a proved implication."
